answer.worked:
The cylinder top and exposed annulus together form a circle of radius $3\ \mathrm{cm}$.

$$\begin{align*}
A_{\text{top-facing}} &= \pi(2)^2+\bigl[\pi(3)^2-\pi(2)^2\bigr]\\
&=9\pi\ \mathrm{cm}^{2}
\end{align*}$$

$$A_{\text{cylinder curved}}=2\pi(2)(3)=12\pi\ \mathrm{cm}^{2}$$

$$A_{\text{hemisphere curved}}=2\pi(3)^2=18\pi\ \mathrm{cm}^{2}$$

$$\begin{align*}
A_{\text{total}} &=9\pi+12\pi+18\pi\\
&=39\pi\\
&\approx122.5\ \mathrm{cm}^{2}
\end{align*}$$
